# Modular code structure

Prefer focused modules over growing god-files (`App.tsx`, large panels, fat CSS).

## Hard limits
- **Every script/source file: max 200 lines** (see `script-line-limit.mdc`). Split before exceeding.
- Prefer files under **~200 lines**; never grow a file past 200 without extracting first.
- New pure logic belongs in `src/domain/` with colocated `*.test.ts`.
- Shared non-domain helpers go in `src/utils/`.
- Reusable React state machines go in `src/hooks/`.
- Presentational UI shells go in `src/components/` with props in, callbacks out.
- Styles live in `src/styles/*` and are imported from `src/App.css` (do not re-monolith CSS).

## App.tsx role
`App.tsx` is the composition/controller root only: own project/room/selection state, `commitProjectChange`, and wire extracted components/hooks. Do not dump new ribbon/status/modal JSX or pure helpers back into it. Prefer orchestration hooks (`useProjectFileIo`, `useRoomOperations`, etc.) when App grows.

## Extraction order when a file grows
1. Pure helpers / domain functions
2. Presentational components
3. Hooks for history, I/O, shortcuts, storage-backed libraries
4. Keep orchestration and selection mutation in the controller until those hooks stabilize

## Folder pattern
For multi-concern domains, use a folder with `index.ts` re-exports (see `projectRooms/`, `projectReview/`, `desktopUx/`, `technicalViews/`).
